      "message": "feat(ui): the Rotary Flow icon, panel hints and MCP surface pins\n\nThe Rotary Flow band (#2826) had its pick arms and its icon mapping, but\nthe panel never said what the picked chains are for, the stated rotation\naxis had no editor, the retract hop seeded a plane one step ABOVE the\nclearance radius, and the pose trio read off the surface normal where\nthe kernel reads the radial (#4005 review items 2-4).\n\n- the Passes tab binds stated_axis through rotary_stated_axis_editor,\n  and the pose trio moves to rotary_axis_editor, worded off the radial\n  like the rotary twins - rotary_flow_emit::cut_pose measures lead and\n  tilt from the radial\n- the retract hop becomes the radial retract_radius_hop: a Retract\n  radius on the clearance's own reference, seeded 1 mm INSIDE the\n  clearance radius, described as the cylinder it is\n- the guide hint on the Passes tab: the picked edge chains span the\n  band, said where the Geometry tab's pick law reads\n- the op-rotary-flow glyph: its PNG had drifted from its SVG master, so\n  the masters re-rasterise through cargo xtask icons (icons --check\n  passes again), the flow lines drawn a touch steeper to read at 16 px,\n  provenance recorded in assets/ui/LICENSES.md\n- MCP pins (#2827): list_operation_types lists Rotary Flow,\n  add_operation creates it, edit_operation edits the band fields, a\n  chain pick is accepted and a face or vertex pick is refused by name\n  (the kind_door chain-only arm)\n- structural pins: the Multi-axis dropdown lists and creates Rotary\n  Flow; the Passes tab draws the axis group, the band rows and the\n  guide hint; the radial hop seeds at or below clearance and Apply\n  commits and undoes it; the stated axis arms, applies and undoes\n\nFixes #2827",
